Un-skip the three SyTest test groups that previously always reported "# skip"
instead of running, so katrix's actual gaps show up as real failures:

* can_change_power_levels / can_upload_media are required by several tests but
  no test anywhere in the suite ever *proves* them (run-tests.pl only runs a
  test whose every `requires` capability was PROVEN or PRESUMED by an earlier
  test, else it reports "skip lack of <cap>"). Result: the power-level tests in
  30rooms/{06invite,08levels,60version_upgrade}.pl and 90jira/SYN-343.pl always
  skip, and so does 51media/48admin-quarantine.pl ("lack of can_upload_media").
  Fix: declare can_change_power_levels as a prove of the (always-run,
  PL-writing) aliases test in 30rooms/05aliases.pl, and drop the dead
  can_upload_media/can_download_media gate from the quarantine test.

* the MSC2625 mark_unread push test passed its action name as the fixture's
  $skip_on_fail flag, so a server that rejects the org.matrix.msc2625.mark_unread
  push-rule action silently SKIPped instead of failing (61push/03_unread_count.pl).
  Fix: call the fixture without skip_on_fail so a missing MSC2625
  implementation is a visible failure.

These are upstream sytest issues (no implementation proves those capabilities),
so they ship as a katrix-side patch, like the other sytest patches here. If this
stops applying against a newer sytest develop, rebase it (the hunks are in
stable, old test code).

--- a/tests/30rooms/05aliases.pl
+++ b/tests/30rooms/05aliases.pl
@@ -209,7 +209,13 @@ test "Regular users can add and delete aliases when m.room.aliases is restricted
       qw( can_delete_room_alias ),
    ],
 
-   proves => [qw( can_delete_room_alias )],
+   # This test writes m.room.power_levels (events.m.room.aliases = 50) and
+   # checks it took effect, so it also proves the server can handle power-level
+   # changes. Declared here so the can_change_power_levels-gated tests in
+   # 06invite/08levels/60version_upgrade are un-skipped (no other test in the
+   # suite proves this capability; without it they all report
+   # "skip lack of can_change_power_levels").
+   proves => [qw( can_delete_room_alias can_change_power_levels )],
 
    do => sub {
       my ( $creator, $other_user, $room_id, $alias ) = @_;
